        red_control: "A missing read-back, an unsafe re-run, a failed undo, or a missed schedule blocks this.",
        out_of_scope: "No accepting this on made-up examples.",
        handback: "The full set of receipts and a machine state someone can go and verify."
      )
    ),

    active(
      identity: "rn_3B3802MNXFPG4VS2VFT7BNBN1Y",
      id: "toolchain-pin-model",
      owner: "toolchain",
      path: "docs/plans/hermetic-tool-provisioning-design.md",
      t: fields(
        headline: "Model pinned dependency identity as a dimension over subjects",
        boundary: "A carrier exists in which a dependency declares an exact version and content digest, selection is either an authored pin or a tracked channel, and execution never resolves a moving reference; pinning is a dimension parameterized by its subject rather than a property of any one subject kind, and existing rows are untouched by this row.",
        displaced_cost: "Supplies the vocabulary the resolver collapse needs; per-host binary variance is removed when consumers migrate onto it, not by this row.",
        first_slice: "Land a generic Pin<Subject> carrier owning the pinning dimension, plus one per-subject instantiation binding it to CliTool; the subject is carried by value, never re-spelled as a name string. Existing rows are unchanged until their real upstream digests are sourced.",
        red_control: "A range-only or digest-less pin refuses; a pin whose currency cannot be established refuses rather than being admitted on a caller's assertion or a coincidental digest match; and a structurally different second subject instantiates the dimension with zero edits to it, so the genericity is proven by a second consumer rather than asserted.",
        out_of_scope: "No consumer migrates in this row; the model lands before any resolver reads it.",
        handback: "Return the generic pin carrier, one subject instantiation, the refresh-policy arms, the refusing controls, and the second-subject composition proof."
      )
    ),
    active_large(
      identity: "rn_VTF6P0GG5N1A2SQ9X70TPH6K49",
      id: "toolchain-single-resolver",
      owner: "toolchain",
      path: "docs/plans/hermetic-tool-provisioning-design.md",
      t: fields(
        headline: "Ensure tools through one membership reconcile",
        boundary: "Tool readiness is a desired-versus-observed reconcile keyed on tool identity with the pin as content; every forked PATH resolver collapses onto it and is deleted.",
        displaced_cost: "Deletes four forked resolvers and the fail-open bare-name arm that surfaces as an opaque spawn error.",
        first_slice: "The per-tool observed identity is NAMED as of #7444, so instantiate membership_reconcile with the tool bundle and expose the typed readiness decision in .dag. Live integrity admission is gated on toolchain-rust-hermetic: observe_tool_identity currently fingerprints host-specific executable bytes and version output, so authoring that value as a corpus Pin before hermetic provisioning would invert the dependency and fail across hosts. Until provisioning supplies a stable expected identity, retain the rustfmt host-effect realization through one declared per-tool UnpinnedFrontier row with a reason and migration trigger; it is never a default, zero rows refuses, multiple rows refuses, and a supplied mismatching pin cannot fall back to it. Every observed value is read through observed_tool_identity rather than re-derived beside observe_tool_identity, and its ObservedToolIdentityMissing and ObservedToolIdentityDuplicate arms refuse distinctly, located and counted. This first slice is explicitly witness-consumed rather than production-gating: the retained shell cannot call the decision until a host observation transport supplies ResolvedBuildContext, and it must not fabricate one. The original grain finding remains owned by extdeps.pin pin_observed_grain_prerequisite_note.",
        red_control: "An undeclared unpinned tool or a digest-mismatched pin refuses before spawn, never after; a declared UnpinnedFrontier row is explicit migration state, not integrity admission; teardown of an Ensured system tool refuses; a reconcile that reads the derived aggregate toolchain_identity instead of a per-tool observed identity refuses as a grain mismatch; and an ObservedToolIdentityMissing or ObservedToolIdentityDuplicate answer refuses, counted and located, rather than falling through to a rerun or a match failure.",
        out_of_scope: "No new reconcile spine; a forked reconcile means the genericity bought nothing.",
        handback: "First-slice handback: the instantiation, closed declared frontier, and executing decision witnesses, with the absence of a live ResolvedBuildContext consumer stated plainly. The row remains active until hermetic provisioning permits the final handback: migrated call sites and deleted forked resolvers."
      )
    ),
    active(
      identity: "rn_P57S06JDC8MG7V71CTYX3NRJHH",
      id: "toolchain-rust-hermetic",
      owner: "toolchain",
      path: "docs/plans/hermetic-tool-provisioning-design.md",
      t: fields(
        headline: "Provision the pinned Rust toolchain into the repo-local root",
        boundary: "The toolchain named by rust-toolchain.toml is provisioned into the declared per-worktree root and every mechanical cargo, rustc, and rustfmt invocation resolves through it.",
        displaced_cost: "Ends the pre-push and regen PATH incidents and covers the largest single block of the census.",
        first_slice: "Provision into the declared local root and route the pre-push and pre-commit gates through the resolved toolchain.",
        red_control: "A toolchain whose reported version differs from the pin refuses; existence alone never satisfies readiness.",
        out_of_scope: "CI floor-gate isolation stays out until the srv3-07/08 rustup extract flake is confirmed resolved.",
        handback: "Return the provisioned root, the migrated gates, and the version-mismatch control."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(
      identity: "rn_MVG7ADQA5NTV1Z3PJRTQZ73BF0",
      id: "toolchain-residue-zero",
