        boundary: "System-required and bootstrap tools are a short declared set with asserted versions and an ownership that refuses teardown; nothing outside the declared floor is depended on ambiently.",
        displaced_cost: "Makes the remaining ambient surface small, named, and observable instead of assumed.",
        first_slice: "Declare the bootstrap and system tiers and assert them at startup.",
        red_control: "An undeclared ambient dependency reds; a floor member below its asserted version refuses rather than proceeding.",
        out_of_scope: "No C toolchain is shipped; cc and the linker remain declared system requirements.",
        handback: "Return the declared floor, the startup assertion, and the undeclared-dependency control."
